WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.837
-President Trump and Kim Jong-un
met in Singapore Tuesday

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.907
for the first-ever summit
between an American president

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.475
and a North Korean leader.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:12.045
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:16.649
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:18.584
No matter your feelings
on Donald Trump,

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:21.187
he is currently attempting
diplomacy over war,

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.589
which is undeniably
the better option.

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:26.892
That said, I do have some
concerns based on some things

00:00:26.892 --> 00:00:28.427
Donald Trump did
and said yesterday

00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.129
and also based on the fact
that he is Donald Trump.

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:31.463
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.463 --> 00:00:33.633
For example, Trump has managed
this summit very much

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.969
like a made-for-TV spectacle,
fueling speculation

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:38.004
about whether
it would even happen or not.

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:40.807
Minting commemorative coins,
writing dramatic letters,

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:43.510
and staging photo ops
with game-show-sized envelopes.

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.978
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:47.180
Look at that -- it looks
like Trump is auditioning

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.415
to be the next mascot for Gmail.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.418
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:53.286
And the media
has responded in kind.

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.488
Yesterday, for example,
they spent the day

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.790
obsessively tracking
Kim Jong-un's whereabouts

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:00.559
in Singapore as he made his way
about the town.

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:03.329
-Kim Jong-un, someone who rarely
leaves his own country --

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.498
this is the furthest
he's ever traveled --

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:08.200
is out and about on the town
in Singapore.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:11.804
-Kim Jong-un to be out strolling
the streets of Singapore.

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:14.874
-Now you see him walking around
the streets of Singapore.

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:16.509
He has crowds of people.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:20.279
I could see across the road lots
of people taking photos of him,

00:01:20.279 --> 00:01:21.514
waving at him.

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:22.949
-We don't know whether
he's going back

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:26.686
to the St. Regis Hotel
or for another stop,

00:01:26.686 --> 00:01:29.689
but clearly, you know, the night
is young for Kim Jong-un.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.324
-As you saw there,
he was walking into

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:34.526
the Marina Bay Sands,
a very popular hotel

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:35.995
that has a casino inside of it.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:38.531
-Kim Jong-un hanging out
at a nightclub in Singapore.

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.566
-Good Lord.

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:40.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:43.436
Why not just make
an old-timey newsreel?

00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:46.205
"Ah, Singapore,
the jewel of the Orient.

00:01:46.205 --> 00:01:48.575
Folks here are all a-flutter
about the upcoming summit.

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:49.776
Why, who's this?

00:01:49.776 --> 00:01:51.577
It's none other than
North Korean dictator

00:01:51.577 --> 00:01:55.147
Kim Jong-un taking a break
from torturing his own people

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:58.117
to pose for a few snaps with
American businessman Don Trump.

00:01:58.117 --> 00:02:00.186
Shake it away, boys!"

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.487
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:09.495
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:12.932
Imagine being in that nightclub.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:17.703
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:19.005
"Is that Kim Jong-un?"

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:21.140
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:22.741
Now, in the run-up
to this meeting,

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:25.144
Trump admitted that he wasn't
doing much to prepare.

00:02:25.144 --> 00:02:27.613
Later, he tried to back away
from that comment,

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:29.949
and, as usual, rambled his way
into talking about

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:32.485
the 2016 election
and Hillary Clinton.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.586
-I didn't say that.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.421
I said I've been preparing
all my life.

00:02:35.421 --> 00:02:37.757
I always believe in preparation.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.825
But I've been preparing
all my life.

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:43.262
You know, these one-week
preparations, they don't work.

00:02:43.262 --> 00:02:46.666
Just ask Hillary what happened
to her in the debates.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:49.335
-Oh. So Trump prepared
for this summit

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:52.104
the same way he prepared
for the debates.

00:02:52.104 --> 00:02:54.507
What was that meeting like?
Just three hours of Trump

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.409
stalking Kim Jong-un
around a room?

00:02:56.409 --> 00:03:02.181
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:05.184
What happens when
the world's slowest pursuer

00:03:05.184 --> 00:03:08.554
chases the world's slowest prey?

00:03:08.554 --> 00:03:11.758
Tonight on "Planet Earth --
Sloth Versus Slug."

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.225
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:15.327
So, Trump admitted he didn't
prepare for the summit.

00:03:15.327 --> 00:03:17.196
The key question
going into the meeting was this.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.831
How would he know
if it was a success?

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.466
What does success even entail?

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:23.169
And was asked that question over
the weekend at the G7 in Canada,

00:03:23.169 --> 00:03:25.438
and his answer
did not inspire confidence.

00:03:30.509 --> 00:03:32.578 line:0%
-That's a good question --
How long would it take?

00:03:32.578 --> 00:03:35.882
I think within the first minute,
I'll know.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:39.719
Just my touch, my feel.
That's what I do.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:42.088
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:44.690
-Touch and feel
is not how you determine

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:46.959
the success of a summit.

00:03:46.959 --> 00:03:48.727
Touch and feel
is how you determine

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:51.097
whether a blouse
is made of cotton.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:54.567
-♪ The touch,
the feel of cotton ♪

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:59.238
♪ The fabric of my life ♪

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:02.275
-So Trump said he'd know
if Kim was serious

00:04:02.275 --> 00:04:04.644
from his touch and feel,
and yesterday we got to see

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:06.846
that touch and feel
with their first handshake.

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:09.047
The first handshake
and photo op in history

00:04:09.047 --> 00:04:11.350
with a North Korean leader
and an American president.

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.052
And I'm sorry,
but why can't these guys

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.721
find a suit that fits them?

00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.522
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:17.790
Look at that.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:22.795
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:26.099
They look like they shop at a
store called Business Pajamas.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.203
Looks like a promo picture
for a movie called

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.004
"Honey, I Shrunk the Dictators."

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:33.706
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:36.442
Trump and Kim then sat down
for a one-on-one meeting,

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.910
and look at Kim's face.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:41.380
Is it just me, or is even he
confused at how he got here?

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:42.881
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:44.850
It looked like they
got set up on a blind date

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.152
by their weirdest friend.

00:04:46.152 --> 00:04:47.853
Oh, what?
They were?

00:04:47.853 --> 00:04:51.257
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:56.128
In fact, just when you thought
it couldn't get any crazier,

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:58.731
Dennis Rodman was there
in Singapore for the summit,

00:04:58.731 --> 00:05:01.134
and he was interviewed on CNN
wearing a MAGA hat

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:03.770
and a shirt
for something called PotCoin.

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:04.970
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.306
I'm pretty sure PotCoins
are what you have to eat

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:08.975
to hallucinate that interview.

00:05:08.975 --> 00:05:10.109
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.410
Especially when,
for some reason,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.381
Rodman thanked his agent,
former Bulls coach Phil Jackson,

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.217
and Pearl Jam frontman
Eddie Vedder.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:19.551
-Can I thank some people,
though, while I'm here?

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:20.820
Can I thank some people?

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.956
All the good people that
stood by me, Darren Prince,

00:05:23.956 --> 00:05:25.457
you know, Vo,

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:27.560
all the guys that went with me
to North Korea.

00:05:27.560 --> 00:05:29.095
You know,
I'm thanking Chuck Daly,

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.264
I'm thanking Phil Jackson,
I'm thanking Jeanie Buss,

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.799
I'm thanking Pete Ginopolis,

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.266
I'm thanking Eddie Vedder,
Pearl Jam,

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:36.969
everybody that's supported me
all through all these things.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.804
-Chris Cuomo
does pretty good there

00:05:38.804 --> 00:05:40.506
until his eyebrows
shoot up to his hairline.

00:05:40.506 --> 00:05:42.141
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.141 --> 00:05:45.511
Man, the news these days really
feels like a Mad Lib from 1999.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:53.986 line:0%
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:57.790
In fact,
after watching the summit,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.559
you might actually think
you O.D.'d on PotCoins

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:02.061
from how often Trump,

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.462
a man who has fought
with everyone

00:06:03.462 --> 00:06:04.730
from allies to war heroes,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.567
complimented brutal dictator
Kim Jong-un.

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:17.943 line:0%
-Very good.
Very, very good.

00:06:17.943 --> 00:06:20.045
Excellent relationship.
Thank you.

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:21.814
He's got a great personality.

00:06:21.814 --> 00:06:23.516
He's a, you know, funny guy.

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:26.252
He's a very smart guy.
He's a great negotiator.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:40.967
Well, he is very talented.
Anybody that takes over

00:06:40.967 --> 00:06:43.836
a situation like he did
at 26 years of age

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:48.508
and is able to run it,
and run it tough.

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:50.610
-What are you talking about?

00:06:50.610 --> 00:06:52.378
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.378 --> 00:06:54.747
This is a guy
who starves his own citizens

00:06:54.747 --> 00:06:57.683
and assassinates people
with antiaircraft guns.

00:06:57.683 --> 00:07:00.620
You're talking about him like
he started Apple in his garage.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.787
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.787 --> 00:07:03.088
But I guess it shouldn't
surprise me that

00:07:03.088 --> 00:07:05.290
Trump's idea of talent is
getting rich by taking over

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.592
your dad's business.

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:07.960
Trump was born on third base,

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.762
whereas Kim was born
on third base,

00:07:09.762 --> 00:07:11.397
and then shot the third baseman.

00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:12.931
[ Laughter ]

00:07:12.931 --> 00:07:15.034
In fact, Trump seemed as
interested in looking forward

00:07:15.034 --> 00:07:17.402
at potential business
opportunities in North Korea

00:07:17.402 --> 00:07:20.440
as he was in getting Kim
to give up his nuclear weapons.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:23.376
-As an example,
they have great beaches.

00:07:23.376 --> 00:07:24.877
You see that whenever
they're exploding

00:07:24.877 --> 00:07:26.145
their cannons into the ocean.

00:07:26.145 --> 00:07:27.179
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.179 --> 00:07:28.313
I said,
"Boy, look at that beach.

00:07:28.313 --> 00:07:30.683
Wouldn't that make
a great condo behind?"

00:07:30.683 --> 00:07:32.884
And I explained, I said, "You
know, instead of doing that,

00:07:32.884 --> 00:07:35.754
you could have the best hotels
in the world right there.

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.123
Think of it
from a real-estate perspective."

00:07:38.123 --> 00:07:41.894
-He accidentally told
a great [bleep] joke.

00:07:41.894 --> 00:07:45.164
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.164 --> 00:07:46.165
I mean...

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:51.671
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:53.105
..."They have great beaches.

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:54.807
You can see it
when they're exploding

00:07:54.807 --> 00:07:58.577
their cannons into the oceans"
is a great [bleep] joke.

00:07:58.577 --> 00:08:00.112
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.112 --> 00:08:02.381
That would be like me
coming to work today and saying,

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:04.817
"I accidentally
signed a treaty."

00:08:04.817 --> 00:08:08.520
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:10.756
Even when he's in the middle of
a summit over nuclear weapons,

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:14.026
he's still trying to sell
a [bleep] hotel timeshare.

00:08:14.026 --> 00:08:15.794
"If you give up
your nuclear weapons now,

00:08:15.794 --> 00:08:18.431
you can stay one night free at
my new Trump Hotel Pyongyang."

00:08:18.431 --> 00:08:20.166
[ Laughter ]

00:08:20.166 --> 00:08:21.533
But again,
diplomacy with North Korea

00:08:21.533 --> 00:08:23.335
is undeniably --
it's a good thing.

00:08:23.335 --> 00:08:24.770
It is a very good thing.

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.706
It's vastly preferable
to fiery rhetoric

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:28.006
and threats of nuclear war.

00:08:28.006 --> 00:08:30.075
The problem isn't that Trump
is engaging in diplomacy.

00:08:30.075 --> 00:08:32.278
The problem is that he doesn't
know what he's doing

00:08:32.278 --> 00:08:33.512
and only cares about optics.

00:08:33.512 --> 00:08:35.481
For example, at their
working lunch yesterday,

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:37.650
Trump asked photographers
to make sure

00:08:37.650 --> 00:08:39.085
he and Kim looked good.

00:08:39.085 --> 00:08:41.487
But watch Kim's face
after Trump's comment.

00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:48.861 line:0%
-Beautiful.

00:08:48.861 --> 00:08:52.063
-[ Speaking Korean ]

00:08:52.063 --> 00:08:54.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:54.934 --> 00:08:58.771
-Okay. So now here I can --
If you are wondering, I can --

00:08:58.771 --> 00:09:00.172
There's an explanation here.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:03.509
You see,
he's a ruthless dictator.

00:09:03.509 --> 00:09:06.846
That was the first time he's
ever heard that he's not thin.

00:09:06.846 --> 00:09:09.515
[ Laughter ]

00:09:09.515 --> 00:09:10.750
You're looking at a 10-time

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:13.019
"People's Republic"
Sexiest Man in the World.

00:09:13.019 --> 00:09:17.155
[ Laughter ]

00:09:17.155 --> 00:09:19.258
In fact, Trump is apparently
so obsessed with the optics

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:20.592
of this summit
that his White House

00:09:20.592 --> 00:09:22.594
made an action-movie trailer
for the meeting

00:09:22.594 --> 00:09:24.697
and played it for reporters
before his press conference.

00:09:24.697 --> 00:09:26.398
Trump even said
he showed the trailer

00:09:26.398 --> 00:09:28.167
to Kim Jong-un on an iPad.

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:32.771
Again, this is a real video
made by our White House.

00:09:32.771 --> 00:09:34.707
♪♪

00:09:34.707 --> 00:09:38.743
-7 billion people
inhabit planet Earth.

00:09:38.743 --> 00:09:40.279
Of those alive today,

00:09:40.279 --> 00:09:43.849
only a small number
will leave a lasting impact.

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:48.087
Destiny Pictures presents
a story of opportunity.

00:09:48.087 --> 00:09:52.591
A new story, a new beginning,
one of peace.

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:57.763
Two men, two leaders,
one destiny.

00:09:57.763 --> 00:10:01.266
Featuring President Donald Trump

00:10:01.266 --> 00:10:04.603
and Chairman Kim Jong-un

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:07.873
in a meeting to remake history.

00:10:07.873 --> 00:10:09.742
-Is that
an official White House video

00:10:09.742 --> 00:10:12.378
or a direct-to-DVD movie
starring Steven Seagal?

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:14.213
[ Laughter ]

00:10:14.213 --> 00:10:15.648
"The White House is under siege,

00:10:15.648 --> 00:10:19.518
and only one President turned
karate master can stop them.

00:10:19.518 --> 00:10:21.519
Steven Seagal stars
as President Trump

00:10:21.519 --> 00:10:22.788
in 'Tae Kwon Donald.'"

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:25.190
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.190 --> 00:10:27.727
Of course, when President Obama
said he would meet

00:10:27.727 --> 00:10:29.294
with North Korea
without pre-conditions,

00:10:29.294 --> 00:10:31.297
Republicans mocked him
as naive and incompetent,

00:10:31.297 --> 00:10:33.899
but, today, Trump supporters
are showering him with praise.

00:10:33.899 --> 00:10:35.968
In fact, Trump even seemed
to make a major concession

00:10:35.968 --> 00:10:38.136
to North Korea,
apparently without running it by

00:10:38.136 --> 00:10:40.405
military officials
or South Korea first.

00:10:40.405 --> 00:10:42.541
He promised to stop
joint military exercises

00:10:42.541 --> 00:10:43.642
in the region.

00:10:43.642 --> 00:10:45.710
Trump explained
his decision this way.

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:48.280
-We call them war games,
and I call them war games,

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:50.215
and they're
tremendously expensive.

00:10:50.215 --> 00:10:53.686
The amount of money that
we spend on that is incredible.

00:10:53.686 --> 00:10:56.122
We fly in bombers from Guam.

00:10:56.122 --> 00:10:57.489
I said --
When I first started, I said,

00:10:57.489 --> 00:10:58.924
"Where do the bombers
come from?"

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:02.862
Guam, nearby.
I said, "Oh, great, nearby.

00:11:02.862 --> 00:11:05.363
Where's nearby?"
"6 1/2 hours."

00:11:05.363 --> 00:11:07.299
6 1/2 hours?
That's a long time

00:11:07.299 --> 00:11:12.504
for these big, massive planes
to be flying to South Korea

00:11:12.504 --> 00:11:15.140
to practice, and then
drop bombs all over the place,

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:17.242
and then go back to Guam.

00:11:17.242 --> 00:11:19.111
I know a lot about airplanes.

00:11:19.111 --> 00:11:22.715
[ Laughter ]

00:11:22.715 --> 00:11:25.116
-You know a lot about airplanes?

00:11:25.116 --> 00:11:27.185
Because people who know
a lot about airplanes

00:11:27.185 --> 00:11:28.888
don't have to say,
"I know a lot about airplanes."

00:11:28.888 --> 00:11:30.088
[ Laughter ]

00:11:30.088 --> 00:11:31.857
If you got on a flight,
you would be worried

00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:33.792
if you heard your pilot say,
"We're expecting some

00:11:33.792 --> 00:11:35.560
light turbulence
on our way to sunny Florida.

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.830
Should take about 3 1/2 hours.
Thanks for flying Delta.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.331
I know a lot about airplanes."

00:11:39.331 --> 00:11:41.467
[ Laughter ]

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:44.469
Again, diplomacy, so much better
than threats of war,

00:11:44.469 --> 00:11:46.371
and if this summit
ratchets down the tension,

00:11:46.371 --> 00:11:47.606
then that's a good thing.

00:11:47.606 --> 00:11:49.341
We just have to hope
Trump doesn't mess it up,

00:11:49.341 --> 00:11:51.176
because when it comes
to messing things up...

00:11:51.176 --> 00:11:52.177
-That's what I do.

00:11:52.177 --> 00:11:53.812
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:53.812 --> 00:11:57.616
[ Cheers and applause ]

